  <prompt>
    Implement FR-08 (version-stamp + re-anchor-on-stale). Version-stamp EVERY save with the SPE eTag + the
    projection schema version; assert the stamp before applying the operation log. If the base has MOVED
    (the persisted eTag/schema-version no longer matches the load-time stamp), do NOT fail with an eTag 500
    — instead RE-ANCHOR the operation log via `Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs`: the AUTO band
    applies confident re-anchors; REVIEW + ORPHAN results SURFACE for review (never silently dropped). Only a
    genuinely un-re-anchorable operation becomes an ORPHAN that surfaces — no operation is ever silently lost.

    Modify `Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs` (the save path). Re-anchor/version summary state (NOT the
    document bytes) is cached via `IDistributedCache` per ADR-009 — MUST NOT use `IMemoryCache`. Reuse
    `AnnotationReanchorService.cs` (a KEEP asset) as the fuzzy re-anchor layer — do NOT reimplement bands.
    The SPE hop stays behind `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007) — no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`.
    `Services/Compose/` stays pure (ADR-013 Tier-1 NetArchTest green). Every save/load change carries a
    through-the-wire seam slice (ADR-038; the concurrency seam slice is task 054).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 engineer on `ComposeService` + the SPE facade write + the Open XML operation applier.
    Understands that Word regenerates paraIds on external tracked-change saves (design D2 / §5.6 pitfall),
    so a stale base must re-anchor via fuzzy bands rather than fail — and that no operation is ever silently
    dropped (the AnnotationReanchorService contract).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A save path where every save is version-stamped (SPE eTag + projection schema version) and asserted before
    apply; a stale base RE-ANCHORS the operation log via `AnnotationReanchorService` (AUTO applies, REVIEW/ORPHAN
    surface) instead of throwing an eTag 500; and an un-re-anchorable operation surfaces as an ORPHAN, never
    silently dropped. Re-anchor/version summary state uses `IDistributedCache` (not `IMemoryCache`); the SPE hop
    stays behind `SpeFileStore`; `Services/Compose/` stays pure.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 (save + concurrency): "version-stamp every save (SPE eTag + projection schema version); assert
      before applying; if the base moved, re-anchor the op log via `AnnotationReanchorService` (AUTO apply /
      REVIEW+ORPHAN surface) instead of failing." Design D2 + §5.6 pitfall: Word regenerates paraIds on external
      tracked-change saves, so `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy match is the cross-Word-session / stale-base
      fallback (a MUST rule in spec). This task depends on 032 (both legacy writers retired; the unified Patch
      Engine is the sole write path) so re-anchoring targets one applier. The eTag-sequencing for create-on-save
      (051) and the HTTP 423 lock protocol (052) build on this same save path.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — the save path: version-stamp (SPE eTag + projection schema version); assert before apply; re-anchor the op log on a stale base via AnnotationReanchorService instead of failing</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — KEEP asset: fuzzy re-anchor bands (AUTO/REVIEW/ORPHAN) + ambiguity guard + never-silently-drop; REUSE as the stale-base / cross-Word-session fallback</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs — task 030/032 unified Patch Engine (the sole write path the re-anchored op log applies through)</file>
      <file role="dependency">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — SPE eTag read/write stays behind this facade (ADR-007)</file>
