  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (bff-api + docx + spe; xhigh; sonnet). Load the knowledge files + bff-extensions.md + design §5. Read `ComposeService.cs` save path + `AnnotationReanchorService.cs` bands. State the Placement Justification. Run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Version-stamp the save">Stamp every save with the SPE eTag + the projection schema version; persist the summary stamp via `IDistributedCache` (ADR-009, not `IMemoryCache`). Assert the stamp before applying the operation log.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Re-anchor on stale base">When the persisted eTag/schema-version no longer matches the load-time stamp, re-anchor the operation log via `AnnotationReanchorService`: AUTO band applies; REVIEW/ORPHAN results are collected to surface. Do NOT throw an eTag 500.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Surface ORPHANs, never drop">Ensure an un-re-anchorable op becomes an ORPHAN that surfaces for review — never silently dropped or placed. Apply the re-anchored + AUTO ops through the unified Patch Engine; write via the SPE `If-Match` path.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify + size/CVE report">`dotnet build`; run existing `Services/Compose` unit tests + Tier-1 NetArchTest. Publish; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable`. (The through-the-wire concurrency seam slice is task 054.)</step>
    <step order="5" name="Index + deviations">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation (esp. the cross-Word-session paraId regen boundary if it fired) in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The cross-Word-session paraId REGENERATION boundary — if a stale base cannot be re-anchored because Word regenerated the paraIds wholesale on an external tracked-change save, and the fuzzy bands cannot confidently re-anchor a material fraction of the op log, STOP and escalate per root §6 rather than surfacing a document as mostly-ORPHAN silently. This is a known judgment boundary (design D2 / §5.6), not a case to improvise past.</trigger>
  </escalation>

